Z||000000||FieroRyan||09-21-2001||02:05 AM||||What is the exact color of your paint job?  How much did it cost (if you don't mind telling me)?  Where'd you get it done?<P>I love it, I think it would look really really good on mine...  just wanting to know more information to see if it's a possibility for me  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><BR>Thanks!<P><BR>P.S.  I would have PM'd this, but it was a dead link when I clicked it...  sorry.||||reg||1
Z||000001||MinnGreenGT||09-21-2001||10:39 AM||||FieroRyan-<P>The color is officially "Medium Metallic Green" from a '95 Corvette.  I also had gold Pearl added to give it a little nicer "sparkle."  I had a local body shop do the paint (probably would find another though... it's OK...but not a GREAT paint job).  Anyway, I paid about $2200 for paint and some minor bodywork.<P>The wheels are not the stock gold as well, I had them refinished at Precision Wheel Service (PWS) locally for about $100ea. (Color: Ford "Honeywheat" Gold)<P>Just to let you know, I am planning a repaint within the next year or two- and I'm going to go to a slightly lighter, more green color (people often think the car is black, especially if the sun isn't out).  I like the Med. Green color used on the newer GM trucks- still would have them add the gold pearl... that really makes the paint job.<P>Let me know if you have any other questions!<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/strut1.jpg">  <P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig3.jpg">     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/halfpole.gif">   <BR>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett<p>[This message has been edited by MinnGreenGT (edited 09-21-2001).]||||reg||1
